# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
<br>
As a fashion designer, I am committed to creating sustainable and environmentally friendly clothing. This research plan aims to explore the use of eco-friendly materials and production methods in my Parisian fashion concept.<br>
<br>
## Eco-Friendly Materials<br>
<br>
Inspired by The Ordinary&#x27;s approach to skincare, I propose using plant-based materials such as bamboo or sugarcane for the fabric of my collection. These materials are biodegradable and require less water and energy to produce than traditional fabrics.<br>
<br>
## Production Methods<br>
<br>
I plan to investigate sustainable production methods such as 3D printing or digital knitting, which can reduce waste and minimize environmental impact. I will also research local and responsible suppliers who share my commitment to sustainability.<br>
<br>
## Interview Questions<br>
<br>
* What are the most significant challenges facing sustainable fashion designers today?<br>
* How can we incorporate eco-friendly materials into our designs without compromising on style or quality?<br>
* What role do you think sustainable fashion can play in reducing waste and minimizing environmental impact?<br>
<br>
```<br>
